WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.960
The axon has been chosen.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.460
What keeps dendrite proteins from wandering into it?

3
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:14.290
The first few tens of micrometres of the axon form the axon initial segment.

4
00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:19.773
Under its membrane sits a dense coat, built on a scaffold called ankyrin G.

5
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:25.953
Ankyrin G binds beta-IV spectrin, which links it to rings of actin under the

6
00:00:25.953 --> 00:00:26.953
membrane.

7
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:33.507
Through its ANK repeats, it also binds sodium channels, KCNQ2/3 potassium channels

8
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.007
and neurofascin-186.

9
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.420
The initial segment has two jobs.

10
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.420
The first is electrical.

11
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:46.103
A high density of sodium channels, among other features, gives it a low threshold.

12
00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:50.683
So in many neurons, this is where the action potential starts.

13
00:00:51.683 --> 00:00:57.303
In 1999, Bettina Winckler, Paul Forscher and Ira Mellman tested whether the membrane

14
00:00:57.303 --> 00:00:58.663
itself is divided there.

15
00:00:59.633 --> 00:01:04.433
They attached small beads to membrane proteins, and dragged them with a laser trap.

16
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:08.443
the cell body and dendrites the beads moved freely.

17
00:01:09.263 --> 00:01:11.283
At the initial segment they were held back.

18
00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:14.223
The hold depended on actin.

19
00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:16.583
How the barrier works is still argued.

20
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:18.983
Now test the scaffold.

21
00:01:20.043 --> 00:01:22.903
Lower ankyrin G after the initial segment has formed.

22
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.203
The axon is already chosen.

23
00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.187
What happens to the initial segment?

24
00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:32.407
And does MAP2, the dendrite protein, stay out of the axon?

25
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.310
In 2008, Kristian Hedstrom, Yasuhiro Ogawa and Matthew Rasband did this.

26
00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:47.033
The initial segment fell apart.

27
00:01:48.053 --> 00:01:49.493
MAP2 spread into the axon.

28
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:55.517
Near the cell body, the axon began to look like a dendrite, with dendritic spines.

29
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:58.717
Farther out, it kept axonal proteins.

30
00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:02.277
So identity has to be actively held.

31
00:02:03.197 --> 00:02:05.857
Near the cell body, the initial segment holds it.

32
00:02:06.677 --> 00:02:09.117
Farther out, something else does, not yet identified.

33
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:15.567
In 2008, Frank Bradke's laboratory, with Susana Gomis-Rüth and Corette Wierenga,

34
00:02:15.847 --> 00:02:17.247
made the mature neuron's cut.

35
00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:23.187
When the stump was shorter than 35 micrometres, a dendrite became the axon.

36
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.187
Longer stumps regrew.

37
00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:30.157
The authors linked this to stable microtubules in the distal axon.

38
00:02:30.877 --> 00:02:32.537
They did not test the initial segment.

39
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.400
So a young neuron's cut reopens the race easily.

40
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:42.270
A mature neuron's cut reopens it only when almost the whole axon is removed.

41
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.520
One caution: this was all in a dish.

42
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.660
In the brain, the race may be tilted or skipped.

43
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:54.860
In the developing cortex, the trailing process of a migrating neuron often becomes

44
00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.860
its axon.

45
00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:02.470
One pathway is clearly required there: the kinase LKB1, and the SAD kinases it

46
00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.470
activates.

47
00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:09.843
Cortical neurons lacking LKB1, or both SAD kinases, fail to form axons.

48
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:13.353
An axon is won in a race, then held.

49
00:03:14.253 --> 00:03:16.713
Loosen the hold, and the axon can lose features.

50
00:03:17.653 --> 00:03:20.113
Cut almost all of it away, and the race reopens.
